    "body": "On that page the 0xA2 is HIDP-Hdr from the Bluetooth HID profile and not the report ID. You don't have to worry about including this byte, the operating system takes care of it. However, for DS4's output report 0x11 it needs to be included when computing the CRC32 checksum.",
